{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>When one commits a trespass.</b> מְעִילָה everywhere means none other than alteration, as it says ״וַיִּמְעֲלוּ בֵאלֹהֵי אֲבֹתֵיהֶם וַיִּזְנוּ אַחֲרֵי אֱלֹהֵי עַמֵּי הָאָרֶץ״ (II Chronicles 5), and so it says concerning the suspected wife: ״וּמָעֲלָה בוֹ מָעַל״ (Numbers 5)." "<b>And sins unintentionally against the holy things of HaShem.</b> That he derived benefit from consecrated property. And where was he warned? חֵטְא is said here, and חֵטְא is said elsewhere concerning terumah: ״וְלֹא יִשְׂאוּ עָלָיו חֵטְא״ (Leviticus 22) — just as there he was warned, so here he was warned. If you say: just as there he was warned only concerning eating, so here too he was warned only concerning eating — Scripture says ״תִמְעֹל מַעַל״ — it multiplies (Sifra)." "<b>The holy things of HaShem.</b> Those specially designated for the Name — excluding lesser consecrations (ibid.)." "<b>A ram.</b> A term of strength, as in ״וְאֶת אֵילֵי הָאָרֶץ לָקָח״ (Ezekiel 17); so here too strength — a two-year-old (Sifra)." "<b>In your valuation of silver shekels.</b> That it be worth two sela'im."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:08.984971433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}